"""Biological Capability Universe, Phase 1: real external evidence providers.

The previous phase proved a capability gap can drive a search. It searched fifteen claims, so
"nothing found" said almost nothing. This connects a real external index and asks whether the
epistemology survives contact with it:

    desired function -> capability gap -> external evidence search -> physical capability -> recompile

**Build authorization: Phase 1 only.** No universal knowledge graph, no indiscriminate ingestion, no
catalogue of all drugs, genes or molecules, no docking, no molecular simulation, no clinical
prediction, no therapeutic ranking, no invented probabilities.

**Retrieval is not grounding.** Finding a source does not create a capability. Seven states are kept
apart and none implies the next: a source found, a source verified, a claim extracted, a claim
grounded in it, a capability candidate, a capability entitled for the required context, and a
grounded capability.

Retrieval and compilation are separate steps. The networked tool writes a versioned corpus snapshot;
the compiler reads only that, so the same snapshot gives the same verdict and continuous integration
needs no connectivity. Queries pass the repository's case-identity guard and therapy filter before
they leave, and the snapshot stores abstracts only — which bounds what can be grounded, and is said
so in every report.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

EXTERNAL_PRINCIPLE = (
    "The model may propose where to look. The source establishes what was observed. The grounding "
    "layer establishes what may be claimed. Deterministic code establishes whether the capability "
    "satisfies the gap. A negative result is always bounded by the searched universe."
)
